Innovus version 25.1
RTL2GDS Course version 7.0

Staged MMMC physical-design flow using the Stylus Common UI
============================================================

Start one Innovus Stylus session from the physical-design directory:

    cd /home/icd1/workspace/counter_design_45nm/physical_design
    innovus -stylus

Do not start with plain "innovus". That opens the Legacy UI in Innovus 25.13;
Stylus commands such as add_fillers are then reported as invalid commands.

To run the complete flow from stage 1 through stage 7 in one session:

    innovus -stylus -files run_full.tcl

If stage 2 creates pins_mmmc.io, edit the generated file and type "resume" in
Innovus. run_full.tcl will then continue with the remaining stages.

Then source one stage at a time. Check each stage before continuing:

    source 1_init_design.tcl
    source 2_floorplan_power.tcl
    source 3_placement.tcl
    source 4_cts.tcl
    source 5_routing.tcl
    source 6_chip_finish.tcl
    source 7_export.tcl

Stage 1 reads the Genus handoff. Stages 2-7 reuse the design already loaded in
memory, so read_db is not called a second time in the same Innovus session.

Each stage still writes a checkpoint. To resume a stage in a new Innovus
session, run only that stage; it automatically reads the previous checkpoint:

    innovus -stylus -files 3_placement.tcl

On the first stage-2 run, Innovus creates pins_mmmc.io and pauses. Edit the
side/layer/spacing assignments, save the file, then type "resume" to finish
stage 2. Later stage-2 runs reuse that file.

Checkpoints are stored in outputs/mmmc. Reports are separated by stage under
reports/mmmc/<stage_name>.

Stage mapping:
    Stage 2 creates a 12.2 x 8.55 um core with 5 um margins for power rings.
    After changing floorplan dimensions, restart run_full.tcl in a fresh session;
    old placement/routing checkpoints still contain the old geometry.

    1 - Design initialization and MMMC handoff
    2 - Floorplanning, I/O assignment and power planning
    3 - Placement and pre-CTS optimization
    4 - CTS/CCOpt and post-CTS timing analysis
    5 - Filler insertion, routing and post-route optimization
    6 - RC extraction and physical checks
    7 - Final DB/netlist/DEF/SDC/GDSII export

PVS metal fill and foundry LVS are intentionally not run because their rule
decks are not included in this project.
